Confirmed. The correct setup for `@ffmpeg/ffmpeg` 0.12.10 in a no-bundler browser app is:

```js
const { FFmpeg } = await import('https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@ffmpeg/ffmpeg@0.12.10/dist/esm/index.js');
const ffmpeg = new FFmpeg();
await ffmpeg.load({
  coreURL: 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@ffmpeg/core@0.12.6/dist/esm/ffmpeg-core.js',
  wasmURL: 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@ffmpeg/core@0.12.6/dist/esm/ffmpeg-core.wasm',
});
```

The ESM core has `export default createFFmpegCore` → `(await import(coreURL)).default` works. And the module worker path is used (no `importScripts`).

Note: `wasmURL` defaults to coreURL with .js→.wasm, so `dist/esm/ffmpeg-core.wasm` is correct automatically. But `mainScriptUrlOrBlob` = coreURL + '#' + btoa(...) is used by emscripten to locate the wasm — with a cross-origin URL that works since emscripten fetches it via `fetch`.

