parts.text:
Confirmed: the core's `_locateFile` decodes the hash and uses `wasmURL`/`workerURL` verbatim. So passing blob URLs for wasmURL works.

So the fix recipe:
```js
const FF_ESM = 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@ffmpeg/ffmpeg@0.12.10/dist/esm/index.js';
const FF_WORKER = 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@ffmpeg/ffmpeg@0.12.10/dist/esm/worker.js';
const FF_CORE_BASE = 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@ffmpeg/core@0.12.6/dist/esm';

async function toBlobURL(url, mime) {
  const r = await fetch(url);
  if (!r.ok) throw new Error(url + ' → HTTP ' + r.status);
  return URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([await r.blob()], { type: mime }));
}

const { FFmpeg } = await import(FF_ESM);
const ffmpeg = new FFmpeg();
await ffmpeg.load({
  classWorkerURL: await toBlobURL(FF_WORKER, 'text/javascript'),
  coreURL:       await toBlobURL(FF_CORE_BASE + '/ffmpeg-core.js', 'text/javascript'),
  wasmURL:       await toBlobURL(FF_CORE_BASE + '/ffmpeg-core.wasm', 'application/wasm'),
});
```

Note: `await import(FF_ESM)` — inside a module in a browser, importing an absolute https URL is fine. But `classes.js` uses `import.meta.url` for the default worker path, which we bypass via classWorkerURL.

One catch: `esm/index.js` does `export * from "./classes.js"` — a **relative** specifier resolved against the jsdelivr URL. ✓

Another catch: does `dist/esm/classes.js` import anything bare? Let me check its imports. I saw `import { CORE_URL, FFMessageType } from "./const.js";`? No — that was worker.js. Let me check classes.js's imports. Earlier output of classes.js didn't show the head. Let me check quickly. Also `const.js` has `CORE_URL = "https://unpkg.com/@ffmpeg/core@0.12.6/dist/umd/ffmpeg-core.js"` as a default — we override it.

Let me verify classes.js imports.

Also: since a single FFmpeg instance is reused and its FS persists, I should clean up files after each conversion. `ffmpeg.deleteFile` exists.

Let me check classes.js head for bare imports.

