Exit 13 = unsettled top-level await. My fake IDB doesn't fire `oncomplete` on the transaction, so `storeOp` never resolves. Let me fix the shim: `storeOp` does:

```js
openDB().then(db => {
  const tx = db.transaction(store, mode);
  const s = tx.objectStore(store);
  const r = fn(s);
  tx.oncomplete = () => res(...);
  ...
})
```

So `tx.oncomplete` is assigned AFTER `db.transaction()` returns. My shim returns an object with `oncomplete: null` and a `_fire()` that I never call. I need to fire it after the current microtask so `oncomplete` is set. Let me auto-fire in a `setTimeout(...,0)` or a chained microtask. Since `oncomplete` is assigned synchronously right after, a `setTimeout(0)` is safe.

Let me fix the shim.

input.newString:
transaction() {
  const tx = {
    objectStore: () => ({
      get(k) { meta.reads++; const b = store.get(k); meta.bytesRead += (b?.byteLength || 0); return { result: b }; },
      put(v, k) { store.set(k, v); meta.writes++; return {}; },
      delete(k) { store.delete(k); return {}; },
    }),
    oncomplete: null, onerror: null,
  };
  setTimeout(() => { if (tx.oncomplete) tx.oncomplete(); }, 0);
  return tx;
},

